<h2>Keeping clients informed during the build</h2>

<p>Winning the job is only the beginning. Construction projects are long. A kitchen renovation might take six weeks. A new build might take six months. During that time, the client is spending the largest sum of money they will ever part with, and they are anxious. They want to know what is happening, what is coming next, and whether the project is on track.</p>

<p>Most builders communicate project updates informally. A quick text here, a phone call there. The problem is that informal communication creates no record, no consistency, and no structure. One client gets daily updates because they are assertive. Another hears nothing for two weeks and starts panicking.</p>

<p>Construction business software with milestone tracking solves this. You define the key phases of each project (site prep, foundation, framing, lock-up, fit-out, handover) and the system sends automated updates when you mark each milestone as complete. The client gets a message: "Great news. Framing is complete and we are on schedule for lock-up next week. Here is a photo of today's progress."</p>

<p>This does three things at once:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>It reduces client anxiety.</strong> People do not mind waiting when they know what is happening. Silence is what causes stress.</li>
  <li><strong>It cuts down on inbound calls.</strong> Every update you send proactively is a phone call you do not have to answer. That saves hours every week.</li>
  <li><strong>It builds trust and generates referrals.</strong> Clients who feel informed and respected become your best marketing channel. They tell their friends. They leave <a href="/blog/get-more-google-reviews">Google reviews</a>. They come back for the next project.</li>
</ul>

<p>Some builders worry that this sounds like too much admin. It is not. You are not writing custom messages for every client. You are tapping a button in your CRM that says "framing complete" and the system sends the update you wrote once. The entire process takes seconds.</p>

